<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE PEOPLE ONTOLOGY, OURS. Ruled v3.0 under LAW #1.

  These questions were recovered from Altify's own labels and they are the right questions,
  but nothing here reads that package at runtime, keys on its version, or degrades when it is
  absent. The text ships as our seed data. The upstream label name is kept as an identity so
  the family guard can assert a shape and so anyone comparing our wording to Altify's can find
  the counterpart — a name we chose to keep, never a dependency we have to satisfy.

  Custom metadata rather than a custom object for the reason the Model Config type gives:
  configuration deploys with the code and is readable without a query against data the running
  user may not have access to. It is also the only shape that carries a shipped default and a
  per-org override in one row, which is what LAW #1 needs and what a package label could never
  give us, because 2,576 of 2,930 ALTF labels are protected and invisible to subscriber Apex.
-->
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <label>AAO People Question</label>
    <pluralLabel>AAO People Questions</pluralLabel>
    <visibility>Public</visibility>
</CustomObject>
